  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1130 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nFor the remainder of this work week, present model agreement\ncontinues to see southwesterly upper-level flow hold over the\nPanhandles thanks to a close upper-level low building off the\nPacific Northwest coast. This flow is expected to leave the\nPanhandle relatively dry with some breezy conditions present\nthanks to a building lee-side low holding across the Southern\nFront Range. Temperatures will also benefit from this\nsouthwesterly flow allowing far a weak warming trend to follow for\nboth Thursday and Friday. As it stands look for afternoon high to\nhold in the mid to upper 60s with lows in the 40s. By late Friday\nhowever, present models do see this flow come to an end with the\npotential arrival of a new trough and its associated cold front.\nAt this time ensembles are not to thrilled on the idea any\nprecipitation with chances this weekend below 10 percent. However,\nbetter chances may follow next Monday as model hint at yet another\nsystem moving across the area. Otherwise, look for cooler\ntemperatures to follow behind the expected front with highs in the\n50s for the weekend.",
